			<img src="12.jpg" />
		</div>
	</div>

	<p>We spent much of the first months of this year preparing to move. Since my grandson, Zach, now
		has a place of his own, Jenny didn't need such a large place. She found one to move into,
		but of course had to sell the old one, first. So we were basically living out of boxes.</p>

	<p>Then, just as the buyers signed the papers, my beloved dog Ella passed away. She'd been
		showing major signs of age, and finally could barely even walk. She died peacefully at home,
		with me and the two other dogs by her side. It was sad but inevitable; don't get a dog if you
		can't bear to lose it! In Ella's case, she had a marvelous doggie life. She spent a year-and-a-half
		on Maui with ocean swims and cows and feral pigs to play with. Few humans can make that boast.</p>

    <img src="14.jpg" />

	<p>Dogs' lives are short (as are those of most of our animal brothers). But as far as we can tell,
		dogs live their lives in the present moment. While dogs can certainly be stressed, as long as
		things are going well they don't seem to worry about what's coming next. That's a lesson I've
		tried to take to heart. Because human lives, while longer than dogs', still seem pretty damn
		short, especially as our ends approach. And that's when it's more important than ever to
		appreciate the hell out of every moment as it happens.</p>

    <img src="15.jpg" />

	<p>Anyway, after taking care of Ella's remains and cleaning up, the other two dogs and I spent
		a week at my ex Michael's apartment, before moving into the new place in Chandler. Which I'm still
		working on, but I have my own attached apartment with bedroom, kitchen, bathroom (with shower!)
		and living room. It's comfortable and the doggies and I are definitely enjoying it!</p>

    <img src="16.jpg" />

	<p>Oh, and a special shout-out to my son, John, who took time out from his own home-remodeling project
		to help carry and arrange my stuff!</p>

	<p>So that's my yearly report. I'm still kicking and will hopefully still be here in 12 months
		for the yearly post! (Not that I intend to not post in between!)</p>

    <img src="17.jpg" />

	<p>Meanwhile, my goal for the future is to continue working with The Resistance to get that
		orange shit-stain out of our White House and out of our lives. Other than that, it's just
		a day at a time: Keeping up with the medical visits and insurance battles while doing my
		best to smile at the antics of my dogs and grandkids.</p>

    <img src="18.jpg" />

